  "solution": {
    "text": "By Fraunhofer diffraction through a circular aperture,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.22</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></math><br /><img src=\"assets\\st0141_628ef3c41710.png\" style=\"width: 380px; height: 145px;\" /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo></math> diameter of pupil&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mtext>0.25</mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext>0.5</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>cm</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>500</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>nm</mi></math>. The first dark ring is formed by the light diffracted from the hole at an angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi></math> with the axis. Viewing distance,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math><math><mo>&#8756;</mo></math>&nbsp;The minimum separation between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> objects <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>D</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>25</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1.22</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>500</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo